TheGreatFlayer: {
	DisplayName: The Great Flayer
	BestiaryEntry1: ""
}

NightmareRoseBoss: {
	DisplayName: Nightmare Rose
	BestiaryEntry1:
		'''
		"Mother Darkness is never too cut-and-dry, and that extends to her motivations and actions.
		Many, many years ago, Mother Darkness took a son under her wing. Nobody knew how old, nobody knew his name.
		To both himself and observers, his destiny was forever postponed, year after year. He had nothing waiting for him in some distant future,
		as all mother darkness needed from him was his warm, bubbly personality to brighten her days and when it served her interests.
		Since word rarely ever escapes the shade world, nobody knew how, when, or even if, certain things developed.
		One thing is known, though. Hekate, the Deity of Witchcraft and Mischief, saw more potential in the boy than his mother did."
		- Transcripts of the late Terníf the Holy.
		'''
	BestiaryEntry2:
		'''
		"The boy had a humanity to him when he wasnt living the sweet life around his mother. He enjoyed observing bugs, designing jewelery, and drawing silt mandalas.
		This, Hekate took the greatest note of during their brief visits to the shade world. This boy had an appreciation for the fleeting, something Hekate often sought out
		in order to find like-minded co-conspirators for their many stunts. On one particular visit to the shade world, Hekate was disguised as a miserly, elderly churl.
		They said to the boy 'You are not loved here. You are merely a tool for her satisfaction. You know this, do you not?' It was on that day that Mother Darkness would no
		longer locate her son in the shade world, as he had left to become an apprentice of Hekate, under the guise of seizing his true potential..."
		- Excerpt from 'Folk Tales of Pherasia: Volume LXXIII', by Uriel XXV.
		'''
}

